---
// A StreamSink lets Rust push many values over time. Dart calls prefetch once,
// gets control back immediately, and then receives a PrefetchEvent as each URL
// finishes, consumed as an ordinary Dart Stream. Drawn as a sequence diagram.
---

<figure class="diagram frb frb-stream">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 300" role="img"
    aria-label="Dart calls prefetch with a list of URLs and a sink, then gets control back immediately. The Rust core then pushes a PrefetchEvent back to Dart as each URL finishes, which Dart consumes as a Stream.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="frbs-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5"
        markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
      </marker>
      <marker id="frbs-arrow-key" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5"
        markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path class="key-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- actors -->
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="60" y="20" width="180" height="46" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="150" y="44">Dart (UI)</text>
    </g>
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="520" y="20" width="180" height="46" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="610" y="44">Rust core</text>
    </g>

    <!-- lifelines -->
    <line class="lifeline" x1="150" y1="66" x2="150" y2="280" />
    <line class="lifeline" x1="610" y1="66" x2="610" y2="280" />

    <!-- the call -->
    <line class="edge" x1="150" y1="100" x2="610" y2="100" marker-end="url(#frbs-arrow)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="380" y="92" text-anchor="middle">prefetch(urls, sink)</text>

    <!-- control returns immediately -->
    <line class="edge back" x1="610" y1="128" x2="150" y2="128" marker-end="url(#frbs-arrow)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="380" y="120" text-anchor="middle">returns at once, UI keeps running</text>

    <!-- streamed events -->
    <line class="edge cross" x1="610" y1="178" x2="150" y2="178" marker-end="url(#frbs-arrow-key)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="380" y="170" text-anchor="middle">sink.add(PrefetchEvent &#123; index: 0 &#125;)</text>
    <line class="edge cross" x1="610" y1="212" x2="150" y2="212" marker-end="url(#frbs-arrow-key)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="380" y="204" text-anchor="middle">sink.add(PrefetchEvent &#123; index: 1 &#125;)</text>
    <line class="edge cross" x1="610" y1="246" x2="150" y2="246" marker-end="url(#frbs-arrow-key)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="380" y="238" text-anchor="middle">… one per URL, as it finishes</text>

    <text class="bracket" x="724" y="216" text-anchor="end">Dart sees a Stream</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Dart calls <code>prefetch</code> once and gets control straight back. The sink keeps delivering a
    <code>PrefetchEvent</code> per URL afterward, which Dart consumes as an ordinary <code>Stream</code>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  figure.frb-stream .lifeline {
    stroke: var(--rule);
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  figure.frb-stream .edge.back {
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  }
  figure.frb-stream .edge.cross {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  figure.frb-stream .key-head {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }
  figure.frb-stream .bracket {
    font-size: 12px;
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
